      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1770307213936,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🚀 Project Overview\nA modern, enterprise-grade Human Resource Management System (HRMS) designed to streamline workforce management.\n It functions similarly to Odoo HR, offering role-based access for Admins and Employees to manage attendance, payroll, \n, and profiles.\n\n🛠 Technology Stack\nFrontend\nFramework: Next.js 16 (App Router, Server Components)\nLanguage: TypeScript\nStyling: Tailwind CSS v4 + Shadcn/UI (Radix Primitives)\nAnimations: Framer Motion\nIcons: Lucide React\nCharts: Recharts (for analytics and reporting)\nState Management: React Query (TanStack Query v5) for efficient server-state management.\nBackend\nDatabase: PostgreSQL (hosted on Neon Serverless)\nORM: Prisma v6 (Handling schema & migrations)\nAuthentication: NextAuth.js v5 (Beta) (Secure sessions & RBAC)\nReal-time: Socket.io (for instant notifications & updates)\nEmail: Nodemailer (for communications)\n✨ Key Features\n1. Admin Dashboard\nReal-time Overview: Vital stats like Total Employees, Attendance Rate, On Leave, and Payroll expenses.\nInteractive Charts: Visualizations for daily attendance trends and department distribution.\n2. Employee Management\nCentral Directory: View all employees with filtering by department (Engineering, HR, Sales, etc.).\nProfiles: Detailed employee profiles including role, salary, and joining date.\nOnboarding Status: Track active vs. onboarding employees.\n3. Smart Attendance System\nLive Tracking: Real-time Check-In / Check-Out logging.\nAuto-Status: Automatically calculates statuses: Present, Late, Half-Day, Absent.\nExport: One-click CSV Export for daily attendance logs.\n4. Payroll & Finance\nSalary Structure: Manages Base Salary, HRA, Allowances, and Deductions.\nAutomated Calc: Auto-calculates Net Salary based on defined structures.\nBudgeting: Admin tool to track allocated budget vs. actual payroll expenses.\nPayslips: functionality to process salary and export payslips.\n5. Leave Management\nWorkflows: Employees request leave -> Admins Approve/Reject.\nStatus Tracking: Visual badges for leave types (Sick, Casual, Unpaid).\n6. Notifications\nReal-time Alerts: System-wide notifications for important updates (e.g., Leave Approval, Payroll Processed).\n📂 Project Architecture\nThe project follows a modular SaaS architecture:\n\napp/(dashboard): Protected routes for the main application app.\napp/api: Robust API endpoints handling logic for attendance, employees, and stats.\nprisma/schema.prisma: A highly relational database schema connecting Users, Employees, Attendance, and Payroll.\ncomponents/ui: Reusable, accessible UI components ensuring design consistency.\nThis system is built to be scalable, secure, and user-friendly, providing a complete solution for modern HR needs.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🚀 Project Overview\nA modern, enterprise-grade Human Resource Management System (HRMS) designed to streamline workforce management.\n It functions similarly to Odoo HR, offering role-based access for Admins and Employees to manage attendance, payroll, \n, and profiles.\n\n🛠 Technology Stack\nFrontend\nFramework: Next.js 16 (App Router, Server Components)\nLanguage: TypeScript\nStyling: Tailwind CSS v4 + Shadcn/UI (Radix Primitives)\nAnimations: Framer Motion\nIcons: Lucide React\nCharts: Recharts (for analytics and reporting)\nState Management: React Query (TanStack Query v5) for efficient server-state management.\nBackend\nDatabase: PostgreSQL (hosted on Neon Serverless)\nORM: Prisma v6 (Handling schema & migrations)\nAuthentication: NextAuth.js v5 (Beta) (Secure sessions & RBAC)\nReal-time: Socket.io (for instant notifications & updates)\nEmail: Nodemailer (for communications)\n✨ Key Features\n1. Admin Dashboard\nReal-time Overview: Vital stats like Total Employees, Attendance Rate, On Leave, and Payroll expenses.\nInteractive Charts: Visualizations for daily attendance trends and department distribution.\n2. Employee Management\nCentral Directory: View all employees with filtering by department (Engineering, HR, Sales, etc.).\nProfiles: Detailed employee profiles including role, salary, and joining date.\nOnboarding Status: Track active vs. onboarding employees.\n3. Smart Attendance System\nLive Tracking: Real-time Check-In / Check-Out logging.\nAuto-Status: Automatically calculates statuses: Present, Late, Half-Day, Absent.\nExport: One-click CSV Export for daily attendance logs.\n4. Payroll & Finance\nSalary Structure: Manages Base Salary, HRA, Allowances, and Deductions.\nAutomated Calc: Auto-calculates Net Salary based on defined structures.\nBudgeting: Admin tool to track allocated budget vs. actual payroll expenses.\nPayslips: functionality to process salary and export payslips.\n5. Leave Management\nWorkflows: Employees request leave -> Admins Approve/Reject.\nStatus Tracking: Visual badges for leave types (Sick, Casual, Unpaid).\n6. Notifications\nReal-time Alerts: System-wide notifications for important updates (e.g., Leave Approval, Payroll Processed).\n📂 Project Architecture\nThe project follows a modular SaaS architecture:\n\napp/(dashboard): Protected routes for the main application app.\napp/api: Robust API endpoints handling logic for attendance, employees, and stats.\nprisma/schema.prisma: A highly relational database schema connecting Users, Employees, Attendance, and Payroll.\ncomponents/ui: Reusable, accessible UI components ensuring design consistency.\nThis system is built to be scalable, secure, and user-friendly, providing a complete solution for modern HR needs.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
